<title>USA: HealthRite in merger talks, exec resigns.</title>
<headline>HealthRite in merger talks, exec resigns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>HealthRite Inc said Thursday that it is engaged in preliminary discussions with a company in the nutritional supplement industry relating to a business combination or merger.</p>
<p>In a press release, HealthRite also said that Bradley MacDonald resigned as president and chief executive officer and that John Teeger, vice chairman and secretary of the company, has been appointed chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Angelo Talluto, former CFO, has been appointed controller of the company and its wholly owned subsidiary, Jason Pharmaceuticals Inc.</p>
</text>
